VERDICT (a): the theorem-form must exclude (i) the single-particle box-mode carrier
  [m1^2 = 4 sin^2(pi/L), f1^2 = 1, chi ~ L^2/4pi^2] and (ii) the HN1 two-atom family;
  the free F^2-analog composite evades the theorem in the density normalization
  (f1^2 -> 0) but violates it in the extensive (space-summed) normalization
  (f1^2 ~ 3L^2/4pi^2 -> inf, chi ~ L^4).  Carrier normalization is load-bearing.
